      "problem": "$\\int ({e}^{x/4}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({e}^{x/4}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x/4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{x/4}-2\\int -\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{e}^{x/4}-2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+C \\\\  & =2(2{e}^{x/4}-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
